[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66121,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dysplastic melanocytic naevus is an acquired naevus in the genital area with architectural and cytological atypia.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66122,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8727/0 Dysplastic naevus</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66123,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F72.2 Melanocytic naevus with severe melanocytic dysplasia</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66124,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> naevus with architectural and cytological atypia</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66125,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66126,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dysplastic melanocytic naevi are usually on the cutaneous labia majora and less commonly on the perineum. Mucosa is not involved {18976416}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66127,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dysplastic melanocytic naevi share many clinical and epidemiological features with atypical genital naevi. They are often &gt;&nbsp;6&nbsp;mm irregularly bordered macules or papules with central pink tones in a background of tan to brown at the periphery {20868400}. Asymmetry is often seen. In patients with dysplastic naevus syndrome, numerous dysplastic naevi can be observed in sun-protected sites such as the anogenital skin, as well as in sun-exposed sites {20868400}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66128,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dysplastic melanocytic naevi are uncommon. They occur most frequently in women of reproductive age (average age: 32&nbsp;years) {28778635; 18976416}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66129,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology is unknown, except for uncommon cases associated with dysplastic naevus syndrome.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66130,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dysplastic melanocytic naevi, like other acquired melanocytic naevi, are associated with activating mutations, most often in <em>BRAF</em> and <em>NRAS</em>. Genital dysplastic naevi are less studied.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66131,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Dysplastic melanocytic naevus is a macular or papular lesion with variable pigmentation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66132,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Dysplastic melanocytic naevi are characterized histologically by the presence of architectural disorder and cytological atypia. Architectural atypia manifests as bridging of junctional nests between adjacent rete ridges and variation in the size, shape, and position of junctional nests. The epidermis often has a slightly papillomatous architecture. A lentiginous junctional component, of variable density, is frequently present at the periphery of the lesion and extends beyond the dermal component (the so-called shoulder phenomenon). There is usually associated concentric eosinophilic fibroplasia in the papillary dermis near the dermoepidermal junction. Pagetoid scatter is not a feature. Randomly distributed mild to moderate cytological atypia can be seen in the melanocytes {18976416}. The dermal component, when present, is formed of bland melanocytes in the underlying papillary dermis. An inflammatory reaction is often present in the superficial dermis accompanying the lesion. A significant lentiginous component, a well-developed shoulder, randomly distributed melanocytic atypia, and a marked inflammatory reaction are features that may help distinguish dysplastic melanocytic naevi from atypical genital melanocytic naevi. There is often histological overlap between dysplastic melanocytic naevus and atypical genital melanocytic naevus, and distinction between them is not always possible.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-02T15:35:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66133,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 455,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-12T17:41:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
